WEBVTT

00:02:28.837 --> 00:02:30.498
Here I come!

00:02:36.612 --> 00:02:39.248
Wow, you look really cute.

00:02:39.248 --> 00:02:40.482
Really?

00:02:40.482 --> 00:02:43.212
Yeah, really. Right?

00:02:45.821 --> 00:02:49.382
This is a traditional festival
costume we have back on Planet Jurai.

00:02:50.626 --> 00:02:52.728
Well, shall we go now?

00:02:52.728 --> 00:02:54.663
But I don't know, Tenchi.

00:02:54.663 --> 00:03:00.669
Everyone else is working there as
vendors, and I am the only one who isn't.

00:03:00.669 --> 00:03:04.540
You deserve a day off, Sasami.
You work hard every day.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:08.067
Besides, Ayeka and the others
are really excited about today.

00:03:10.379 --> 00:03:12.074
Let's go now!

00:03:12.714 --> 00:03:15.410
To your first festival on Earth!

00:03:22.157 --> 00:03:23.920
Yup!

00:03:34.903 --> 00:03:37.633
Tenchi, come on, hurry up!

00:03:44.179 --> 00:03:46.170
Wow!

00:03:50.786 --> 00:03:53.388
Wow! Tell me, Tenchi, what's that?

00:03:53.388 --> 00:03:56.152
Oh, that's the goldfish scooper.

00:03:57.559 --> 00:03:59.117
You wanna try?

00:04:00.896 --> 00:04:02.386
Sure!

00:04:12.774 --> 00:04:14.469
Gotcha!

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.604
Here!

00:04:42.938 --> 00:04:45.073
Hey!

00:04:45.073 --> 00:04:47.507
Oh, it's you, Ryoko!

00:04:49.378 --> 00:04:52.414
So, you're working as
a goldfish scooper too?

00:04:52.414 --> 00:04:54.650
Sort of.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:56.318
How's it going?

00:04:56.318 --> 00:04:58.520
No good, not at all.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.923
Huh? You don't have
any goldfish here, Ryoko?

00:05:01.923 --> 00:05:05.560
How can you expect any customers to
come to a goldfish scooper without goldfish?

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:08.028
I have goldfish right here.

00:05:14.403 --> 00:05:16.803
I don't see any. Where? Where is it?

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.565
Why don't you check it out yourself?

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:44.922
It is a big fish!

00:05:48.937 --> 00:05:51.565
See? I have some for sure.

00:05:56.144 --> 00:05:58.408
My heart is still pounding.

00:05:59.347 --> 00:06:00.582
Damn it.

00:06:00.582 --> 00:06:01.016
"Danger! Condemned!"
Damn it.

00:06:01.016 --> 00:06:06.215
"Danger! Condemned!"

00:06:10.358 --> 00:06:13.428
Bingo! You hit the bull's-eye.

00:06:13.428 --> 00:06:15.630
Step right up, ladies and gentlemen.

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:19.691
The best place to let it all out.

00:06:26.241 --> 00:06:28.732
Great! Nice shot!

00:06:29.678 --> 00:06:34.081
I never imagined I could make
a business out of fun like this.

00:06:41.556 --> 00:06:44.926
Wow, it looks delicious, Kiyone.

00:06:44.926 --> 00:06:48.897
This is a great opportunity for
us to make up our financial deficit!

00:06:48.897 --> 00:06:50.298
That's right.

00:06:50.298 --> 00:06:53.502
Well, I feel kinda hungry now.

00:06:53.502 --> 00:06:55.270
So do I.

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:57.439
Can we have two fried noodles?

00:06:57.439 --> 00:07:00.575
Coming right up! Mihoshi, are you
ready with the shredded cabbage?

00:07:00.575 --> 00:07:03.510
Oh, yes, as much as you want.

00:07:10.285 --> 00:07:13.588
All right, forget the cabbage
and hand me the carrots.

00:07:13.588 --> 00:07:15.283
Okay!

00:07:17.058 --> 00:07:19.526
Huh? How strange.

00:07:22.631 --> 00:07:26.034
This, and this...

00:07:26.034 --> 00:07:27.467
Oh?

00:07:31.173 --> 00:07:33.542
I knew it.

00:07:33.542 --> 00:07:35.844
It's you, isn't it, Ryo-Ohki?

00:07:35.844 --> 00:07:38.779
An unbalanced diet is
not good for you, you know.

00:07:47.789 --> 00:07:50.314
Well, now, this place looks good enough.

00:07:59.568 --> 00:08:01.369
Step right up, everyone.

00:08:01.369 --> 00:08:05.807
Step right up and see
what we have here now!

00:08:05.807 --> 00:08:09.544
What? Oh, no! What is it you have there?

00:08:09.544 --> 00:08:12.180
Now, see this frog
right here in front of you?

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:14.382
This is not a common frog you can find
everywhere, mind you, but a very special one.

00:08:14.382 --> 00:08:15.817
I don't mean that it's special in a way

00:08:15.817 --> 00:08:19.387
like it sticks flat on your shirt
or anything of the sort though.

00:08:19.387 --> 00:08:22.924
What? What do you mean?
In what way is it different then?

00:08:22.924 --> 00:08:24.793
I'm so glad you asked, Miss.

00:08:24.793 --> 00:08:27.421
Now, listen, this frog right here
is not just an ugly common frog...

00:08:28.563 --> 00:08:33.227
...but an inhabitant of Alpha-Centaur
at the bottom of Mount Tsukaba.

00:08:34.069 --> 00:08:37.005
This is the one known by the name of:

00:08:37.005 --> 00:08:39.541
Vasco da Gama!

00:08:39.541 --> 00:08:41.243
Wow! It can't be, can it?

00:08:41.243 --> 00:08:43.545
I never imagined I would be
able to see one with my own eyes!

00:08:43.545 --> 00:08:44.446
And now watch.

00:08:44.446 --> 00:08:45.780
I put this toad in this box of 3-D mirrors,

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:49.050
and see, something strange happens.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:54.852
The toad starts to sweat at the
sight of itself reflected in the mirrors.

00:08:56.791 --> 00:08:59.127
And you can collect all
the drops of its perspiration

00:08:59.127 --> 00:09:01.196
in a ceramic pan and
cook it slowly on a low fire,

00:09:01.196 --> 00:09:06.234
stirring the liquid all the time with an
ultra-compression Techtite stick for 42 days,

00:09:06.234 --> 00:09:11.137
and it cooks down to this, what
you see right here: Gama Vitan Z!

00:09:12.574 --> 00:09:18.113
Anything from bruises and sprains
to crying babies and arterial sclerosis...

00:09:18.113 --> 00:09:20.415
a drop of this miracle
liquid can cure them all!

00:09:20.415 --> 00:09:24.986
You know, I'm suffering
from stiff shoulders and stuff.

00:09:24.986 --> 00:09:26.354
Are you saying that this
thing here can even cure that?

00:09:26.354 --> 00:09:28.290
Of course. It works so well

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:31.226
that your shoulders will
feel as light as feathers.

00:09:31.226 --> 00:09:33.592
You want the proof, just
go ahead and try it yourself.

00:09:37.465 --> 00:09:39.100
Go, go, fight!

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:41.136
Wow! Could this be true? It's like a miracle.

00:09:41.136 --> 00:09:44.230
My shoulders aren't stiff anymore at all!

00:09:46.041 --> 00:09:48.610
Really, they are so light,
you see? Unbelievable!

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:53.281
And I'm offering this Gama Vitan Z
for only 3,000 yen per bottle.

00:09:53.281 --> 00:09:57.385
It costs twice as much
around the Planet Jurai area.

00:09:57.385 --> 00:09:59.220
Really? Really? That's a deal!

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:02.691
You have a real conscientious
way of doing business.

00:10:02.691 --> 00:10:05.455
You have a weird way of talking, I say.

00:10:07.862 --> 00:10:10.031
You just stop cheating, please.

00:10:10.031 --> 00:10:11.199
Oh, my God, that's not true.

00:10:11.199 --> 00:10:14.202
What are you talking about?
I'm not cheating.

00:10:14.202 --> 00:10:16.438
Right?

00:10:16.438 --> 00:10:18.872
Do I look like I'm cheating at all?

00:10:22.944 --> 00:10:24.809
Obviously.

00:10:33.121 --> 00:10:37.285
Oh, it feels so great!

00:10:37.859 --> 00:10:40.555
Hey, can I do that too?

00:10:41.162 --> 00:10:44.063
Just a second. I'll finish in a minute.

00:10:46.735 --> 00:10:50.501
Oh, I may get addicted to this.

00:11:04.352 --> 00:11:06.588
Step right up, folks,
to this Haunted Mansion,

00:11:06.588 --> 00:11:08.490
the best of its kind of all time.

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:10.892
The tricks we have here are
something you've never seen.

00:11:10.892 --> 00:11:15.463
Super technology created by
the best genius in the universe!

00:11:15.463 --> 00:11:17.532
Hello, Washu!

00:11:17.532 --> 00:11:19.830
Oh, you're here at last.

00:11:21.603 --> 00:11:24.105
Haunted Mansion, is it?

00:11:24.105 --> 00:11:27.409
How about popping in and checking it out?

00:11:27.409 --> 00:11:30.111
You'll be impressed.

00:11:30.111 --> 00:11:31.179
I'm sure of that.

00:11:31.179 --> 00:11:33.948
Well, I guess we'll take your invitation.

00:11:33.948 --> 00:11:36.618
All right. A party of two coming in!

00:11:36.618 --> 00:11:38.787
What kind of exhibition do you have in here?

00:11:38.787 --> 00:11:40.021
Just like this:

00:11:40.021 --> 00:11:43.124
Tour the eight worst hells.

00:11:43.124 --> 00:11:45.360
- Oh!
- Sounds so exciting!

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:47.851
Well, enjoy yourselves.

00:11:58.306 --> 00:12:01.142
It's rather small, isn't it?

00:12:01.142 --> 00:12:02.410
It's not surprising.

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:05.346
Washu tends to exaggerate
things anyway, you know.

00:12:05.346 --> 00:12:07.282
So we go inside through this door, I guess.

00:12:07.282 --> 00:12:08.715
I'm so excited!

00:12:09.317 --> 00:12:10.685
Whoa!

00:12:10.685 --> 00:12:14.722
- Wha-What's this?
- Whoa! Ow, ow, whoa!

00:12:14.722 --> 00:12:16.212
Wow.

00:12:26.701 --> 00:12:28.862
Wha-What's this? Where am I?

00:12:29.737 --> 00:12:32.228
Wow, it's a sea of magma.

00:12:36.444 --> 00:12:38.179
Whoa! What's that?

00:12:38.179 --> 00:12:41.282
Could it be the Hellish
Pool of Blood, maybe?

00:12:41.282 --> 00:12:43.250
Looks like it.

00:12:47.322 --> 00:12:49.724
Whew. This is not funny.

00:12:49.724 --> 00:12:51.521
Tenchi.

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:53.752
What's the matter...

00:13:11.913 --> 00:13:14.816
It can't be.

00:13:14.816 --> 00:13:17.216
Th-The Mountain of Needles?

00:13:24.559 --> 00:13:27.357
It looks more like the
Himalayan Mountain of Needles.

00:13:34.669 --> 00:13:36.704
Are you all right, Sasami?

00:13:36.704 --> 00:13:39.172
Y-Yeah, I'm okay.

00:13:41.342 --> 00:13:43.606
Ugh. What was that?

00:13:48.483 --> 00:13:50.974
Tenchi!

00:13:59.194 --> 00:14:01.628
Wow, Tenchi, you're great!

00:14:11.072 --> 00:14:13.836
Step right up, folks! Step right up!

00:14:20.148 --> 00:14:22.884
Wow, you've managed to
come out in one piece, huh?

00:14:22.884 --> 00:14:27.021
Well, we've cleared all eight stages.

00:14:27.021 --> 00:14:28.957
And how was it?

00:14:28.957 --> 00:14:33.360
Scary... more than enough... too scary.

00:14:37.632 --> 00:14:40.902
Hey, you there. Why don't you stop by?

00:14:40.902 --> 00:14:43.905
I have the best thing here
for you to let out all that stress.

00:14:43.905 --> 00:14:47.534
Now, step right up, folks!
Come on, step right up!

00:14:52.547 --> 00:14:55.049
Step right up, folks. Step right up!

00:14:55.049 --> 00:14:57.885
Excuse me, Ryoko, but
what are you doing there?

00:14:57.885 --> 00:15:00.188
Can't you see it's a shooting gallery?

00:15:00.188 --> 00:15:03.558
You deliberately set it up next
to mine to destroy my business!

00:15:03.558 --> 00:15:06.493
Ha! What do I care about that?

00:15:08.763 --> 00:15:11.630
It seems you need more
than words to be convinced.

00:15:14.335 --> 00:15:16.237
Ouch! Ouch!

00:15:16.237 --> 00:15:19.035
- Excuse me, I need it for a moment.
- Wh-What are you doing?

00:15:59.047 --> 00:16:01.072
How dare you?

00:16:05.286 --> 00:16:07.948
- Here you go. Thanks for waiting.
- Wow!

00:16:11.459 --> 00:16:13.861
You're selling cotton candy now?

00:16:13.861 --> 00:16:18.032
Yup. We ran out of the
ingredients for fried noodles.

00:16:18.032 --> 00:16:21.469
I'm sorry. It was Ryo-Ohki's fault.

00:16:21.469 --> 00:16:23.938
It's okay. Would you like one too, Sasami?

00:16:23.938 --> 00:16:27.141
Wow, can I?

00:16:27.141 --> 00:16:30.044
Sure. It's for you.

00:16:30.044 --> 00:16:31.568
Thank you.

00:16:33.014 --> 00:16:34.649
Mmm, it's delicious.

00:16:34.649 --> 00:16:36.640
I'm glad for you, Sasami.

00:16:37.785 --> 00:16:40.955
Now, Mihoshi, we
should sell and sell like this.

00:16:40.955 --> 00:16:42.590
Work hard, and keep making them.

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:44.192
You can count on me!

00:16:44.192 --> 00:16:47.862
With this ultra high-speed cotton
candy maker especially made by Washu,

00:16:47.862 --> 00:16:50.732
I can handle any large quantity of orders.

00:16:50.732 --> 00:16:53.601
Huh? So it was Washu who made that?

00:16:53.601 --> 00:16:55.831
Yes, it was.

00:16:59.741 --> 00:17:01.976
Hey, Mihoshi, watch out!

00:17:01.976 --> 00:17:03.409
Huh?

00:17:03.978 --> 00:17:05.179
Stop the machine, now!

00:17:05.179 --> 00:17:08.171
I-I can't stop it.

00:17:20.595 --> 00:17:25.967
We seem to be bonded
to each other through fairs.

00:17:25.967 --> 00:17:30.927
Yeah, it was at a fair on a planet
in the neighborhood of Jurai.

00:17:32.507 --> 00:17:35.510
Yes, that was my
first time to be out there

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:39.776
among common people
and experience a fair.

00:17:41.082 --> 00:17:44.483
Hey, Missy! You there!

00:17:47.989 --> 00:17:49.724
Huh? Me?

00:17:49.724 --> 00:17:52.093
Yes, you. You're the lucky one.

00:17:52.093 --> 00:17:57.064
I've just got a shipment
of great products. Well, now!

00:17:57.064 --> 00:18:00.301
I'll sell this to you, Missy,
at a special discount price.

00:18:00.301 --> 00:18:02.203
Oh, oh, no. I can't...

00:18:02.203 --> 00:18:04.433
Don't be shy.

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:09.243
You just take this, and
I'll take the money from you.

00:18:09.243 --> 00:18:11.779
Wait! Give me back my wallet, please!

00:18:11.779 --> 00:18:14.849
I don't accept returns.

00:18:14.849 --> 00:18:17.051
Stop telling lies, Ayeka.

00:18:17.051 --> 00:18:19.654
What lies are you talking about, huh?

00:18:19.654 --> 00:18:22.290
What you just said... all of it!

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:25.316
Listen now. I'll tell you
exactly what happened.

00:18:26.127 --> 00:18:30.832
Yes, it was a cold, cold night,
chilling me to the bones.

00:18:30.832 --> 00:18:34.302
I had worked so hard to make
all these with my own hands,

00:18:34.302 --> 00:18:36.429
but no one came to
buy them, no one at all.

00:18:39.073 --> 00:18:41.042
Can I help you?

00:18:41.042 --> 00:18:45.046
Hey, who gave you
permission to do business here?

00:18:45.046 --> 00:18:46.447
Huh?

00:18:46.447 --> 00:18:50.618
This is the fair site to praise
the god for Jurai royal family,

00:18:50.618 --> 00:18:54.956
and I cannot allow you to do
business in here without permission.

00:18:54.956 --> 00:18:56.424
But...

00:18:56.424 --> 00:18:58.949
Ha! Look at this shabby booth!

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:05.700
No! Oh, no. You're so mean.

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:07.935
How dare you make up a story like that?

00:19:07.935 --> 00:19:10.137
Your memory must be completely rotten.

00:19:10.137 --> 00:19:13.374
I'm telling you just the facts, you know.

00:19:13.374 --> 00:19:15.710
Which are the facts in your story?

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:19.614
All of them, everything I said.

00:19:19.614 --> 00:19:21.916
Don't you understand even that much?

00:19:21.916 --> 00:19:25.249
I guess a princess from a royal
family can't understand everything.

00:19:26.387 --> 00:19:32.059
Really, you are hopeless.
It's no use trying to have a talk with you.

00:19:32.059 --> 00:19:33.327
So what?

00:19:33.327 --> 00:19:36.763
I'm ready for revenge, Ayeka, to make
you pay for what you did back then.

00:19:51.379 --> 00:19:55.372
- Wh-Wha...
- Wh-What's going on?

00:20:40.561 --> 00:20:41.963
Sorry, Sasami.

00:20:41.963 --> 00:20:44.065
It was supposed to be
a fun evening at the fair,

00:20:44.065 --> 00:20:45.600
but it turned out to be such a mess.

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:48.302
You must be really disappointed.

00:20:48.302 --> 00:20:51.839
Oh, no, Tenchi. I'm not!

00:20:51.839 --> 00:20:53.739
I'm not.

00:20:55.009 --> 00:20:57.000
Mmm, it's delicious.

00:22:56.263 --> 00:22:58.966
Genius Washu invents Mecha-Washu,

00:22:58.966 --> 00:23:04.305
but she inputs Mihoshi's
personality instead of hers.

00:23:04.305 --> 00:23:05.306
Ahem!

00:23:05.306 --> 00:23:07.007
What are you on your high horse about?

00:23:07.007 --> 00:23:09.276
Washu's ability plus Mihoshi's personality...

00:23:09.276 --> 00:23:12.480
it might be the worst idea in the universe!

00:23:12.480 --> 00:23:14.381
Next episode is: "No Need for a Genius!"

00:23:14.381 --> 00:23:17.985
The battle of Washu versus
Mecha-Washu starts now.

00:23:17.985 --> 00:23:20.215
It's unquestionably wonderful.
